establishing a three-year review and update cycle for the plan thereafter Staff report Chairman and members of finance committee Brenda Maro deputy city treasurer Back in 2013 the governing body adopted resolution 5545 which put in place a requirement for the city to prepare a five-year capital improvement plan each year The idea was to give us a clear strategic tool for prioritizing capital projects like new construction infrastructure improvements or major repairs by laying out the scope cost funding resources and responsible department for each project Well the intent was sound in practice The annual update process has not worked as expected Keeping the plan current every year has required significant staff time and resources but it hasn't provided the level of value or direction for policym and

budgeting that was originally envisioned The resolution before you today makes adjustments to the process so that our capital planning is more practical sustainable and useful Our goal remains the same to give the city and governing body a strong tool for long-term planning but in a way better way in a way that better fits our resources and decision needs And I'll stand for any questions Thank you Any comment from committee questions hearing none Any comment from the public either here or online hearing none Uh may I have a motion uh Mr Chairman I move to adopt this resolution Second Moved by Moody seconded by Esabel Uh any further discussion from the committee hearing none Um all

those in favor say I I Those opposed Uh the recommendation for Monday's meeting will to be to adopt um Madame Clerk Number 15 resolution reappropriating the fiscal year 2025 budget of the city of Cheyenne according to the provisions of Wyoming statute 16-4-112 and 16-4-113 Thank you Staff report Hi uh chairman members of the finance committee can you hear me okay Yes Okay This is Robin Lochman city treasurer Thank you for the opportunity to provide information on the final reappropriation request for last fiscal year While the memo I provided contains full details I want to highlight the key points for the general fund reserves request I am requesting $1,878 $87,984 from general fund reserves to cover a number of items At the same time I estimate that the general fund departments will revert approximately 1.4 million in unspent appropriations for fiscal year 2025 after accounting for encumbrances and

rollover balances which will be reappropriated into the fiscal year 26 budget next month Beyond that I want to also note that the general fund reserves have grown by nearly 12.7 million between July 1st 2024 and June 30th 2025 primarily due to stronger than anticipated uh revenues compared to budget especially in building permits historic horse racing and franchise fees as well as the budget reversions that I just mentioned The majority of the general fund requests reflect the way we manage the budget As I've explained in my memo it is not possible to predict a year in advance the exact costs of items such as employee leave payouts vandalism and theft expenses fuel and utility price fluctuations or accident related costs Rather than setting aside an arbitrary amount in advance and

tying up funds that could be used elsewhere or force departments to cut back on other line items we instead make these adjustments at year end and backfield departmental budgets from reserves as needed In addition to those adjustments there are seven specific requests from general fund reserves First the fire department's overtime costs are over budget by $198,674 However their overall department budget is only short about $14,000 because other line items within the department have surplus funds that cover most of the overtime overage The discrepancy arose because this final reappropriation must be initiated before our year in close at the end of August to allow time for attorney review and the council agenda and approval process Unfortunately we found an error after the resolution was submitted to the clerk's office The error has now been corrected So

council may either approve the resolution as drafted or amend to reduce the fire department's general fund reappropriation request by $184,000 Second I am requesting 109,300 for four used vehicles that were purchased separately for the compliance building inspectors Third we need additional local match in the amount of 150,000 for the FTA transit grant Fourth overtime costs related to the noise and speed enforcement that was approved by the governing body earlier this year in the amount of $13,53 Fifth additional public defender costs beyond what was budgeted in the amount of $6,431 Sixth $6,900 for the Downtown Development Authority Striving Project and finally 80 $8,900 to assist with hosting the Wyoming Association of Municipalities annual conference I am happy to answer any questions on these requests and

